$DIR/main.p:38:10: cannot pass []S{...} to each, which keeps it after returning
    A slice literal (at main.p:38) keeps its elements in an array in f's frame,
    and the slice looks at that array. each passes items to call (main.p:31),
    which passes s to s.String (which may call main.(*S).String) (main.p:23),
    which stores s in package variable keepS (main.p:13), so []S{...} would
    outlive f's frame.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change each to take a value or an owner, which it can keep: an owned[T] from
    new, a shared[T], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
